The individual producer files and image ID match exactly. My first aggregate-tree comparison used the audit-output tree hasher, whose framing differs from the pipeline’s producer-bundle hasher; that produced a non-authoritative mismatch. I’m correcting this with the exact `pipeline_contract.sha256_tree` function used to populate `/audit-input.json` and will preserve both raw results with the distinction documented.
exec
/bin/bash -lc "env PYTHONPATH=/reference python3 - <<'PY'
import json
from pathlib import Path
from tools.pipeline_contract import sha256_tree
bundle = Path(\"/reference/generation-tools\")
audit = json.loads(Path(\"/audit-input.json\").read_text())[\"resolution\"]
observed = sha256_tree(bundle)
expected = audit[\"hashes\"][\"generation_producer_sources_sha256\"]
print(f\"hasher=tools.pipeline_contract.sha256_tree\")
print(f\"observed_producer_tree_sha256={observed}\")
print(f\"audit_input_producer_tree_sha256={expected}\")
print(f\"producer_tree_matches_audit_input={observed == expected}\")
PY" in /audit-output
