diff --git a/evidence/10_operational-adversarial-tests.txt b/evidence/10_operational-adversarial-tests.txt
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..a26fb6b03fca35731d473a9830329389d03fee5d
--- /dev/null
+++ b/evidence/10_operational-adversarial-tests.txt
@@ -0,0 +1,42 @@
+COMMAND
+env ELAN_HOME=/opt/elan LD_PRELOAD=/tmp/audit-work/proc-exe-shim.so lake env lean OperationalAudit.lean
+
+WORKDIR
+/tmp/audit-work/stage5-audit.HfRJIU
+
+EXIT_CODE
+0
+
+COMPLETE_STDOUT_STDERR
+"-120"
+"0"
+[45, 49, 50, 48]
+[65, 66]
+true
+false
+true
+-7
+[65, 66, 43, 42]
+[45, 49, 50, 48]
+[49, 50, 43, 51]
+true
+false
+true
+false
+false
+false
+false
+
+INTERPRETATION OF OUTPUT ORDER
+The first fourteen lines exercise negative/zero integer formatting, ASCII
+conversion, string-code projection, both constructor guards, integer total
+projection on its guarded domain, sequence concatenation, the str built-in,
+string addition, and both K-cast projections.  The final four `false` values
+show that constant Int2String, constant codesProject, left-identity
+seqConcat, and constant-none applyBuiltin counterfactuals are observationally
+different on relevant inputs.  The compiled final example additionally proves
+that an always-failing Int projection cannot satisfy the first cast lemma when
+paired with the correct constructor guard.
+
+SOURCE
+/tmp/audit-work/stage5-audit.HfRJIU/OperationalAudit.lean
